From 6f19494a60cc70695fdd8a7a9e517814938bea7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Revulate <76570121+Revulate@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 12:57:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Bound image URI decoded rasters

A generic URI image can bypass Echo's stricter media decoder, so GPUI's
URI loader bounds what it decodes as well as the transport body: an axis
above 8192 px, more than 64 MiB of RGBA in one frame, more than 256 MiB
of RGBA across all frames, or more than 1,024 frames is rejected.

The limits travel as an `ImageDecodeLimits` into upstream's shared
`decode_gif_image`/`decode_webp_image` helpers, which check the canvas
size before decoding any frame and check every decoded frame as it
arrives. `Image::to_image_data` (files, clipboard) passes no limits.
Other raster formats from a URI are checked from the decoder's
dimensions before decoding.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
